---
description: Before planning or building non-trivial work, run autoscope elicitation
alwaysApply: true
---

When planning (Plan mode, or any request to design, architect, build, or scope
something non-trivial), do NOT invent scope, constraints, acceptance, or
architecture silently.

First use the `autoscope` skill: inspect the repo and existing logs, classify
the task type, and ask only high-impact unknowns in the skill's condensed
format. Only draft the plan or start implementing after those are answered
(or explicitly listed as Assumed).

Skip the checkpoint for small, local changes (a bug fix with clear repro, a
rename, a single function, a typo, a config tweak).
